From f349fd363a2be9c5641326ab7015b6b0b3b6c931 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jordan McCallum <apt-install-coffee@proton.me>
Date: Thu, 20 Aug 2026 16:55:16 +1000
Subject: [PATCH 141/145] v7.2: drop fork subsystems now superseded by mainline

Linux v7.2 upstreamed/redesigned several areas the Sky1 patch set carried:

- drm/panthor: mainline now has GPU CPU/GPU coherency (ptdev->coherent),
  which is what the fork's ACE-Lite patch added. Restore mainline panthor
  and drop the fork's now-redundant GPU coherency changes (incl. the
  re-added panthor_regs.h that v7.2 deleted).
- firmware/arm_scmi: v7.2 rebuilt the SCMI transport layer around
  scmi_transport_supplier. The fork's ACPI-boot SCMI additions no longer
  apply; adopt mainline SCMI (device-tree boot path is unaffected).
- pci/pci-acpi.c: the fork's ACPI resource-fixup approach was already
  reverted within the patch set; restore mainline (v7.2 also needs its
  iommu.h include for pci_dev_reset_iommu_prepare()).

Per maintainer direction: adopt mainline for ACPI subsystems v7.2 redesigned;
the Orion O6 boots via device tree here.
